k3Rdy", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53488, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01A2cicippdZT78DJbgk3Rdy", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54955, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JJR8GFcC32bfhdjyxS9KVW", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55255, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JJR8GFcC32bfhdjyxS9KVW", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55255, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JJR8GFcC32bfhdjyxS9KVW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59535, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 18% to 0.2%. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Diagnosis:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** The first rollback to v2.3.0 stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. I retried once, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, and it finished in us-west and eu-west.\n3. **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate. Creating it pages the on-call engineer.\n\nThe incident lists two follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 is failing.\n- Investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Tz9hcB7GhT9mazrDNuLgyB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VUnoCiui54KcFWatmTP3pe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011mwXGkc8hkZwHAQDYzxTWd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MNESWcsE7vHWGmBV7v2CyX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only finished in us-east. I'll retry it once, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AxfTzEXg6d2QYgWMfnseyE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014kLebhYXtGVkMocfSxeJ5j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EhcvYFq88RkdTNsDL2HpCz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01A2cicippdZT78DJbgk3Rdy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and investigate the orchestrator error during rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JJR8GFcC32bfhdjyxS9KVW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 18% to 0.2%. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Diagnosis:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** The first rollback to v2.3.0 stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. I retried once, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, and it finished in us-west and eu-west.\n3. **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate. Creating it pages the on-call engineer.\n\nThe incident lists two follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 is failing.\n- Investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}